# Restoration Magic's mana value is its mana cost's, {W} = 1, whichever mode is chosen and whatever cost it adds
# (CR 702.183a, 202.3). Cura costs {W}{1} to cast, so counting the mode's cost would make it mana value 2. Bot2's Spell
# Snare ("Counter target spell with mana value 2") has Pyroclasm ({1}{R}, mana value 2) to target, so it is castable, and
# Bot1's Cura on the stack is not among its targets (the refusal); Pyroclasm is the positive control and is countered.
# Cura then resolves: Bot1's Mother of Runes gains hexproof and indestructible and Bot1 gains 3 life.

